# Milestone: M3 (activated v0.14.0-refoundation)
# Covers: a loop body containing `&` is desugared once, not once per
#         iteration.  Both arms of the join fire, and `break` leaves after
#         a single pass -- so exactly two lines come out.  A body
#         re-desugared on each visit would either fork again or fail to
#         fork at all.
#
#         Ported from legacy/repos/aldebaran-urbi/tests/2.x/multiple-visit.chk.
#         Previously a placeholder claiming `&` needed a step driver; it
#         does not.  The join runs on the loader strand like any other
#         chunk-top fork, and `## mode: file` is what gives the whole
#         program one pump instead of one per line.
# matrix-row: separator-and

## mode: file

while(true) { echo(1) & echo(1); break }
[00000000] *** 1
[00000000] *** 1
